Step 2 — Save logic in the app
Goal: every save goes through one routine that records history and updates the derived fields. This is what makes the weekly report possible.
Do this — on every save of a Project, Submission, EffortLog or Note:
1.	Read the current values of the item.
2.	Compare with the incoming values, field by field. Convert both to text the same way before comparing: dates as YYYY-MM-DD, numbers with 2 decimals, people as login names, multi-person sorted and joined with “;”, empty as ““.
3.	If nothing changed, stop.
4.	Save the item.
5.	Write one ChangeLog row per changed field (ChangeType = Create for new items). For Notes, write one row on create only, NewValue = first 200 characters.
6.	Update the parent project’s derived fields (these writes are not logged):
–	NextSubmissionDate / NextSubmissionType = earliest Submission with empty ActualDate and status not Cancelled.
–	LatestNote = newest Note text, first 200 characters.
–	BlockedSince = today when Status becomes Blocked-client; cleared when it changes to anything else.
–	RAG, using the rules below.
7.	If any write fails: retry once, then show an error to the user. Never continue silently.
Tracked fields: - Projects: Stage, Status, StatusReason, CyberProvisioned, CyberPM, DSS_PM, ProjectPM, BudgetMM, Client, Title - Submissions: Type, PlannedDate, ActualDate, SubmissionStatus, Owner - EffortLog: MMConsumed
RAG rules (computed, never typed by a user; first match wins):
RAG	Rule
Red	Any overdue submission, or Blocked-client for more than 14 days
Amber	A submission due within 7 days that is not In progress or Submitted, or Blocked-client for 14 days or less, or effort used is 80% or more of BudgetMM before Detailed Design
Grey	Status is Pending kickoff, On hold, Not awarded or Closed, or the project has no submissions
Green	Everything else
Delete rules: - A Project can be deleted only when Status is Closed or Not awarded. The app deletes its Submissions, EffortLog and Notes first, and writes Delete rows to ChangeLog. - Notes and ChangeLog rows are never deleted.
Blanks: empty, “—”, “-” and “(none)” are all stored as empty and shown as “Unassigned” or “Not assessed”. They are never a category in a chart.
Done when these tests pass: 1. A submission with PlannedDate 6 May and ActualDate 6 May is not overdue. 2. Change a project’s Status to Blocked-client: BlockedSince is set, a ChangeLog row exists, RAG is Amber. 3. Create a project: exactly one ChangeLog row with ChangeType = Create, not one per field.
