Step 3 — Migrate the Excel
Goal: move the existing data into the new lists without polluting the history.
Do this:
1.	Mario exports the Excel to CSV and cleans it: fills missing project numbers with TBD-###, maps stage and status text to the Choice values, splits Cyber PM names into separate people.
2.	For each Excel row create one Projects row.
3.	For each Excel row create Submissions rows: one for “Last Submission” (ActualDate = that date, status Submitted) and one for “Next Submission” (PlannedDate = due date). Where a cell contains several milestones (e.g. 30% CD / 60% SD / 90% DD / 100% IFC), create one row each — Mario will supply these by hand.
4.	Import the Excel “Notes” column as Notes rows (Category Internal, Author Mario, NoteDate = import date).
5.	Run the import with a migration flag so ChangeLog rows are written with Suppressed = Yes.
6.	Run the derived-field update (Step 2, item 6) for every project.
7.	From now on the Excel is read-only. All updates go through the app.
Done when: the Overdue count in the app matches Mario’s manual count, and the “What changed this week” panel (Step 4) shows nothing for the migration week.
