Step 4 — Dashboard and table (first version for management)
Goal: the screens that produce the weekly report. Build in this order.
4.1 Four KPI cards at the top (replace the current four)
Card	Counts
Due this week	Submissions with PlannedDate in the current week and no ActualDate
Overdue	Overdue submissions (definition in Step 1)
Blocked	Projects with Status Blocked-client, plus average days blocked
Unassigned	Projects with no CyberPM or CyberProvisioned = Not assessed
Remove the “Due dates” line chart and the “Overdue by due date” bar chart.
4.2 “What changed this week” panel
Week = Monday 00:00 to next Monday 00:00, Riyadh time. A selector lets the user pick any past week.
1.	Query ChangeLog where ChangedOn is inside the week and Suppressed = No, ordered by ChangedOn.
2.	Group rows by SourceList + ItemID + Field. Take the first OldValue and the last NewValue. If they are equal, drop the group (a change that was reverted in the same week is not reported).
3.	Put each remaining change in a bucket and show buckets as collapsible sections with counts:
Bucket	Rule
New projects	Projects, ChangeType Create
Moved stage	Field = Stage
Blocked	Field = Status, new value Blocked-client
Closed / On hold	Field = Status, new value Closed, On hold or Not awarded
Submitted	Submissions, Field = ActualDate, old empty, new set
Slipped	Submissions, Field = PlannedDate, new later than old
Reassigned	Field is CyberPM, DSS_PM or ProjectPM
Effort booked	EffortLog, total MMConsumed in the week
Other	everything else, collapsed
Each row shows: project, item, field, old → new, who changed it. Clicking opens the project page.
4.3 “Next 14 days” table
Submissions with PlannedDate within 14 days and no ActualDate. Columns: Project, Type, Planned date, Owner, RAG, days remaining, latest note. Sorted by planned date.
4.4 Project table
•	Default columns: RAG, ProjectNumber, Title, Client, Stage, Status, CyberPM, Next submission (type + date), Latest note.
•	Available via column picker: DSS PM, Project PM, BudgetMM, MM consumed, CyberProvisioned.
•	Remove the Modified column.
•	Default sort: Red first, then NextSubmissionDate ascending.
•	Filters: Status, Stage, CyberPM, RAG, CyberProvisioned, Client, title text. Preset “My projects” = CyberPM contains the current user.
•	Inline edit: Status, StatusReason, CyberProvisioned, CyberPM.
•	Clicking any chart segment filters this table and shows a filter chip.
Done when: Mario has reviewed it. This version is shown to management. Nothing in Step 5 starts before this review.
